WEBVTT

00:00:00.050 --> 00:00:03.304
Processing keeps cassava longer, and can earn you more.

00:00:04.150 --> 00:00:07.126
Keep harvested roots in the shade, and move them quickly.

00:00:07.680 --> 00:00:10.145
Peel the roots, and wash them with clean water.

00:00:10.690 --> 00:00:16.940
Many farmers process cassava into gari, fufu or flour, which last much longer.

00:00:17.490 --> 00:00:25.979
Follow proper processing steps, like grating, fermenting, pressing, and drying or roasting. These also make cassava safe to eat.

00:00:26.530 --> 00:00:34.250
Before you move on, check: Keep roots shaded. Process or sell within 2 to 3 days. Use clean water and tools.

00:00:35.000 --> 00:00:37.964
In the next lesson: Selling your produce.
